d\",\"height\":80,\"tag\":null,\"url\":\"https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/506fda37111e6faa7237ad371aa56d4ddc0804e2a3ce610518659d08469ef709/lightyear_networkapi/smartcrop_w80_h80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fd29szjachogqwa.cloudfront.net%2Fimages%2Fuser-uploaded%2Fjasmine-andersson-new_9751.png\",\"width\":80}]}},\"id\":\"1c6d5550-0d55-11ea-bcda-f2fa6e2a42f0\"},\"brandUrl\":\"https://profiles.yahoo.com/brands/yahoo_news/\"},\"badges\":[{\"id\":\"NEWS\",\"type\":\"Category\"}],\"bypassModal\":false,\"cacheId\":\"764f3b26-2923-40ae-9a5c-34ddbf67d034-1790498359454\",\"categoryLabel\":\"News\",\"commentCount\":0,\"contentType\":\"story\",\"id\":\"764f3b26-2923-40ae-9a5c-34ddbf67d034\",\"isHosted\":true,\"isLiveLabelSuppressed\":false,\"liveBlog\":false,\"pubDate\":\"2026-09-24T15:21:11Z\",\"slides\":null,\"summary\":\"Here's how your benefit is worked out and which other limits are changing\",\"thumbnail\":{\"altText\":\"NEW YORK, NEW YORK - OCTOBER 30: An EBT sign is displayed on the window of a grocery store on October 30, 2025 in the Flatbush neighborhood of the Brooklyn borough in New York City.  Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP) benefits and other assistance are set to stop on November 1st amid a federal government shutdown that has been going on for 29 days and is the second-longest shutdown in the nation's history. New York Gov. Kathy Hochul declared a state of emergency for extra emergency funds and personnel to be deployed, as SNAP payments will be suspended. About 42 million Americans are expected to lose access to their benefits. (Photo by Michael M. Santiago/Getty Images)\",\"caption\":\"NEW YORK, NEW YORK - OCTOBER 30: An EBT sign is displayed on the window of a grocery store on October 30, 2025 in the Flatbush neighborhood of the Brooklyn borough in New York City.  Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP) benefits and other assistance are set to stop on November 1st amid a federal government shutdown that has been going on for 29 days and is the second-longest shutdown in the nation's history. New York Gov. Kathy Hochul declared a state of emergency for extra emergency funds and personnel to be deployed, as SNAP payments will be suspended. About 42 million Americans are expected to lose access to their benefits. (Photo by Michael M. Santiago/Getty Images)\",\"originalHeight\":4000,\"originalUrl\":\"https://s.yimg.com/os/creatr-uploaded-images/2025-11/96205cc0-b72d-11f0-bff7-e7b22e832c1b\",\"originalWidth\":6000,\"resolutions\":[{\"__typename\":\"ImageResized\",\"height\":286,\"tag\":null,\"url\":\"https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/eefed8f6885863c7166172c5abecafabe7946cc9d4c0a7f73ed70773925b631a/lightyear_networkapi/smartcrop_w520_h286_faces%3Bquality_85%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fs.yimg.com%2Fos%2Fcreatr-uploaded-images%2F2025-11%2F96205cc0-b72d-11f0-bff7-e7b22e832c1b\",\"width\":520},{\"__typename\":\"ImageResized\",\"height\":260,\"tag\":null,\"url\":\"https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/f93c25cce193cd5f0126a9399aa34b417f877516ecb815ef3f03a7f024f21804/lightyear_networkapi/smartcrop_w260_h260_faces%3Bquality_85%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fs.yimg.com%2Fos%2Fcreatr-uploaded-images%2F2025-11%2F96205cc0-b72d-11f0-bff7-e7b22e832c1b\",\"width\":260}]},\"title\":\"SNAP benefits rise Oct. 1. Here's how much more you could get.\",\"type\":\"story\",\"url\":\"https://www.yahoo.com/news/us/article/snap-benefits-rise-oct-1-heres-how-much-more-you-could-get-152111476.html\",\"viewCount\":0,\"wpm200\":293,\"metadata\":{\"ccode\":\"\"}},{\"attribution\":{\"authorImage\":{\"altText\":\"\",\"originalHeight\":1050,\"originalUrl\":\"https://s.yimg.com/os/creatr-uploaded-images/2025-10/04dea090-a60d-11f0-bfdf-b877b269a460\",\"originalWidth\":1050,\"resolutions\":[{\"__typename\":\"ImageResized\",\"height\":80,\"tag\":null,\"url\":\"https://s.yimg.com/lo/mysterio/api/58565d4e3855671efccfedeadf214931603d0878a721056600ae48a1834dd000/lightyear_networkapi/smartcrop_w80_h80%3Bformat_webp/https%3A%2F%2Fs.yimg.com%2Fos%